{"id":"cfdb0665b498bc958845cd5568394fd5ca7222b6","axis":"silent","repo":"comet-ml/comet-llm","sha":"cfdb0665b498bc958845cd5568394fd5ca7222b6","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"apps/opik-backend/config.yml","lines":["@@ -3059,6 +3059,17 @@ topics:","     #  Default: 5s","     #  Description: How long a stopping pod waits for each of its runs to be put back to queued. At most 1m","     requeueWait: ${TOPICS_RUNS_REQUEUE_WAIT:-5s}","+  # Guards of a trace query filtered by topic (trace list, count and stats, trace KPI cards, trace metrics). ClickHouse","+  # settings on the whole query, only when the filters have a topic. A trip answers 503 with Retry-After","+  filter:","+    #  Default: 30s","+    #  Description: ClickHouse max_execution_time of the query, whole seconds from 1s to 4m. A longer query outlives","+    #  the progress headers the driver can take at the default databaseAnalytics.httpHeadersProgressIntervalMs","+    maxExecutionTime: ${TOPICS_FILTER_MAX_EXECUTION_TIME:-30s}","+    #  Default: 4294967296 (4 GiB)","+    #  Description: ClickHouse max_memory_usage of the query, in bytes; the trace read and the topic subquery together.","+    #  At most 68719476736 (64 GiB)","+    maxMemoryUsage: ${TOPICS_FILTER_MAX_MEMORY_USAGE:-4294967296}","   #  The ClickHouse guards of the read API's reads (counts per topic and day, the collecting count), apart from the","   #  run's: a page request, not a background job. A rows, bytes or memory trip answers status too_large; a time","   #  trip or a spent budget answers 503 with Retry-After"],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/opik-backend/docs/ai-labels-runbook.md","lines":["@@ -244,6 +244,49 @@ with the API, run the query on the same UTC date and at least `CACHE_MANAGER_TOP"," project's last API call, or the API can answer from its cache. A run that saves between the two reads changes the"," counts."," ","+### Traces filtered by topic","+","+The traces list takes a `topic_id` filter. \"View all logs\" on a topic opens the list with it. The value is a topic's","+`id` from this endpoint, or Other's all-zeros id. The field is `STRING_EXACT`, the type of the other id fields: the","+value is compared exactly, and ids are lower case. The page and the Logs chip use `=`. A value that is not an id","+matches no trace. The filter applies to the list and its `total`, to `GET /v1/private/traces/stats`, to the search","+stream (`POST /v1/private/traces/search`), to the trace KPI cards (`POST /v1/private/projects/{id}/kpi-cards`) and to","+the trace metrics (`POST /v1/private/projects/{id}/metrics`, `trace_filters`). `GET /v1/private/projects/stats`","+ignores it: it spans many projects, and a topic belongs to one.","+","+```json","+[{\"field\": \"topic_id\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": \"<topic_id>\"}]","+```","+","+The filter uses the rules of [How it counts](#how-it-counts). Every row counts, each trace goes by its latest row,","+and a topic that is not live is Other. A trace with no counted row fails every operator, `!=` included: `!=` keeps","+only traces that have a topic row, so it is not the opposite of `=`. With topics off, a workspace not opted in or","+listed at a stage before `ui`, or a project with no live topic, the filter returns no trace and no error.","+","+The page's link opens Logs with the time range, which bounds the list by the time in the trace id. The read API counts","+by the trace's `created_at`. So the list's `total` can differ from the topic's `count` for traces whose id time is","+outside the window (late or imported traces), and around UTC midnight. For an exact match, add two `created_at`","+filters, `>=` the start of `window_from` and `<` the start of the day after `today`, both in UTC","+(`2026-10-06T00:00:00Z`), and the Logs page's filters `source = sdk` and `visibility_mode = default`. With these, the","+list's `total` equals the topic's `count`, and with the Other filter, the sum of `other.series`. A run that saves","+between the two requests can change both.","+","+The backend reads MySQL first: whether the workspace is eligible, then the project's live topics. Then each trace","+query gets `AND id IN (<subquery>)`, as score filters do. The subquery reads the project's `trace_topics` rows, keeps","+the latest row of each trace, and returns the ids that pass the filter. It is bounded only by the trace id range of","+the list: its time range and its cursor. With neither, it reads the project's whole history in `trace_topics`. It has","+no `log_comment` of its own: in `system.query_log` it is part of the list's queries (`find_traces_by_project_id`,","+`count_traces_by_project`). The KPI cards and the metrics carry the same subquery, bounded by their own id range.","+","+A query with a topic filter has two guards on the whole query, the trace read and the subquery together:","+`max_execution_time` from `TOPICS_FILTER_MAX_EXECUTION_TIME` (30 s) and `max_memory_usage` from","+`TOPICS_FILTER_MAX_MEMORY_USAGE` (4 GiB). The list, its count, the stats, the KPI cards and the trace metrics have them;","+a query without a topic filter has neither. A query that stops at a guard answers `503` with `Retry-After: 5` (see","+\"Errors\"). The search stream has already sent its status then, so it ends with an error, as for any ClickHouse error.","+A project whose \"All time\" filter trips a guard on every retry needs a narrower date range, or a higher limit if","+ClickHouse has the memory. The time guard takes at most 4 minutes: a longer query outlives the progress headers the","+driver can take at the default `ANALYTICS_DB_HTTP_HEADERS_PROGRESS_INTERVAL_MS`, and fails instead of answering `503`.","+"," ### Errors"," "," | Code | When |","@@ -252,6 +295,7 @@ counts."," | 404 | The project is not in the workspace. |"," | 400 | A request without `project_id`. |"," | 503, `Topics are busy; retry shortly`, `Retry-After: 5` | A query hit its time guard (159), `TOPICS_READ_BUDGET` ran out, or ClickHouse did not answer within the budget and 2 s. The per-day counts of a large project take a fraction of the budget, so this is load, not size. The backend logs a WARN `Topics read is busy` with the workspace and the project. |","+| 503, `Retry-After: 5`, traces filtered by topic | A trace query with a topic filter (list, count, stats, KPI cards, trace metrics) stopped at a guard: time (159, `TOPICS_FILTER_MAX_EXECUTION_TIME`) or memory (241, `TOPICS_FILTER_MAX_MEMORY_USAGE`). A retry can pass. The backend logs a WARN `Trace query filtered by topic hit a guard`. |"," | 429 | More than `RATE_LIMIT_GET_PROJECT_TOPICS_PER_WORKSPACE_LIMIT` requests from one workspace in `RATE_LIMIT_GET_PROJECT_TOPICS_DURATION_IN_SEC` (60 s). |"," | 500 | Any other error. |"," "],"additions":44,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/opik-backend/src/main/java/com/comet/opik/api/filter/Field.java","lines":["@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ public interface Field {","     String COMMENTS_QUERY_PARAM = \"comments\";","     String EXPERIMENT_ID_QUERY_PARAM = \"experiment_id\";","     String EXPERIMENT_IDS_QUERY_PARAM = \"experiment_ids\";","+    String TOPIC_ID_QUERY_PARAM = \"topic_id\";","     String WEBHOOK_URL_QUERY_PARAM = \"webhook_url\";","     String ALERT_TYPE_QUERY_PARAM = \"alert_type\";","     String ENABLED_QUERY_PARAM = \"enabled\";"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/opik-backend/src/main/java/com/comet/opik/api/filter/TraceField.java","lines":["@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ public enum TraceField implements Field {","     EXPERIMENT_IDS(EXPERIMENT_IDS_QUERY_PARAM, FieldType.STRING_LIST),","     SOURCE(SOURCE_QUERY_PARAM, FieldType.ENUM_LEGACY),","     ENVIRONMENT(ENVIRONMENT_QUERY_PARAM, FieldType.ENUM),","+    TOPIC_ID(TOPIC_ID_QUERY_PARAM, FieldType.STRING_EXACT),","     ;"," ","     private final String queryParamField;"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/opik-backend/src/main/java/com/comet/opik/api/metrics/ProjectMetricRequest.java","lines":["@@ -5,10 +5,12